# One canonical host. https://translationcore.com is canonical (the `site` in
# astro.config.mjs and every canonical, hreflang, sitemap and JSON-LD URL).
# www → apex is NOT done here: Pages ignores domain-level rules in this file.
# It is the zone Redirect Rule `www_to_apex` (see docs/deployment.md).

# Addresses of the previous translationCore site (the Netlify version,
# archived in archive/old-site/), so existing links keep working.
# /translation-helps/#translation-words etc. still land on the right section:
# the fragment survives the redirect, and resources/ keeps those anchors.
/translationcore     /desktop/    301
/translationcore/*   /desktop/    301
/tc4                 /desktop/    301
/tc4/*               /desktop/    301
/translation-helps   /resources/  301
/translation-helps/* /resources/  301

# /home was the homepage of an older site. Google still crawls it (Search
# Console listed it as a 404 in Nov 2026), so send it to the new homepage.
/home                /            301
/home/*              /            301

# The static test build used .html file names; Pages would serve the
# extensionless form, but these send them straight to the canonical
# trailing-slash URL in one hop.
/index.html             /                   301
/desktop.html           /desktop/           301
/mobile.html            /mobile/            301
/resources.html         /resources/         301
/training.html          /training/          301
/previous-version.html  /previous-version/  301
/license.html           /license/           301
/privacy.html           /privacy/           301
